 "tier1Summary": "Europe won a place, if not yet a face, in the Ukraine talks. In Dublin leaders agreed a team of EU officials plus France, Germany, the UK, Italy and Poland, but no single envoy. Money is the harder fight: [[p:Friedrich Merz]] ties the 2028–34 budget to shared Ukraine funding, and Prague and Bratislava refuse. Hungary still blocks Ukraine's last clusters, and gas storage enters winter at a 13-year low.\n\nAt home, the Dutch cabinet wobbles, France's budget sits with the Senate, Sweden waits on the Centre Party, and Spain's right leads before the 29 Nov vote.\n\nElsewhere, [[p:Volodymyr Zelenskyy]] says Washington floated NATO membership for Donbas, Iran claims a strike in Bahrain, and Trump wants Cuba \"done\" before 2029.",
